  "control_definitions": {
    "bound_starts": "Use at least two relative guest orientations/placements for each host stoichiometry. Ring topology is fixed by the host graph; no optimized complex is supplied.",
    "host_deletion": "At each bound geometry remove all host atoms without relaxing guest coordinates; retain guest charges +2/+4 and the same aqueous embedding.",
    "partner_deletion": "For CB8:(G1)2 additionally remove guest B then guest A, giving the two +2 single guests at their frozen bound positions, both with and without CB8.",
    "free_guests": "Relax isolated G1 and G1_2 independently in the same solvent. Compare confinement-induced geometry and excitonic coupling separately.",
    "state_character": "Define fragments host/guestA/guestB before comparing NTOs; inspect whether host-centered or charge-transfer states enter the window."
  },
  "observable_definition": "Compare transition energies/oscillator strengths and matched guest transition densities at identical guest coordinates for full-host, deleted-host and deleted-partner controls. Bright/dark splitting is E(bright)-E(dark) with both state identities recorded; host deletion measures combined host response, not purely electrostatics.",
